This is proprietary, source-available software. The source code is published
so that anyone may READ it. Publication does not make it free or open-source
software, and grants no right of use.


1. YOU MAY, without asking

   a) Read the source code.
   b) Study it and learn from it.
   c) Evaluate it -- for example, when assessing the author's work.
   d) Quote it in a comment, article or review, with attribution to the
      author and a reference to its origin.


2. YOU MAY NOT, without the author's prior written permission

   The following are prohibited with respect to the whole or any part of this
   software, including any single file or fragment:

   a) Using or running it, commercially or otherwise.
   b) Copying or reproducing it.
   c) Modifying, adapting, translating it, or creating derivative works.
   d) Distributing, publishing, or otherwise making it available to others.
   e) Sublicensing, selling, renting or assigning it.
   f) Incorporating it into any other program, product or service, whether
      proprietary, free or open-source.
   g) Using it as training material for machine-learning models.
   h) Removing, obscuring or altering authorship and copyright notices.


3. REQUESTING PERMISSION

   Open an issue on the repository, or contact the author through his GitHub
   profile:

       https://github.com/rayshadow89

   Reasoned requests get an answer. A default "no" does not mean the answer
   has to be no.


4. ABOUT GITHUB FORKS

   While this repository is public, the GitHub Terms of Service grant every
   GitHub user the right to view and fork it within the platform itself. The
   author cannot disable that function on a public personal repository, and
   waives nothing by its existence.

   Forking is NOT permission. A fork remains subject to this licence: it
   authorises no use, no modification, no redistribution outside GitHub, and
   no presentation of the work as one's own.


5. WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

   Stated plainly to avoid misunderstanding. This licence covers the CODE as
   written: its form, its structure, its expression.

   It does NOT cover the ideas, concepts, methods or principles underlying
   the program. Those are not protectable by copyright, and Spanish law says
   so expressly for software (Royal Legislative Decree 1/1996, article 96.4).
   Anyone may write their own personal assistant on the same ideas, provided
   they write it themselves.


